WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.447
- My name's Ashley and
today, I'm gonna test some

00:00:02.447 --> 00:00:06.312
of the most pinned Halloween
foods from Pinterest.

00:00:06.312 --> 00:00:09.564
Every year, Pintrest rounds
up their top most viral pins

00:00:09.564 --> 00:00:11.949
for the Halloween season,
and I picked three

00:00:11.949 --> 00:00:14.330
of those food items that
I'm gonna make today,

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:15.845
to see if it's really worth it.

00:00:15.845 --> 00:00:16.867
Do they look really cute?

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:17.941
Do they taste really good?

00:00:17.941 --> 00:00:20.700
And are they practical to make?

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.114
Now, I am not a chef by any means.

00:00:23.114 --> 00:00:26.045
I am pretty far from it,
but I am an avid Pinner.

00:00:26.045 --> 00:00:28.770
They claim to be that
anybody can make these,

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:30.330
and you can totally
make them and bring them

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.163
to your next party.

00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:32.549
I'm gonna see if that's true. (laughs)

00:00:32.549 --> 00:00:34.248
(mystical chimes)

00:00:34.248 --> 00:00:37.280
The first recipe that I'm
doing are these Pizza Skulls.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.357
You know pizza rolls that
you make in the microwave?

00:00:39.357 --> 00:00:41.323
Imagine a really big version of that

00:00:41.323 --> 00:00:43.675
and it is shaped like a skull.

00:00:43.675 --> 00:00:44.508
Let's do it!

00:00:44.508 --> 00:00:45.934
First step is to unroll the pizza dough

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:48.947
and press into a five
by 10 inch rectangle,

00:00:48.947 --> 00:00:51.356
and cut into six strips.

00:00:51.356 --> 00:00:53.154
That's not a rectangle.

00:00:53.154 --> 00:00:55.374
Oh my gosh, what was
when all the continents

00:00:55.374 --> 00:00:56.246
were put together?

00:00:56.246 --> 00:00:57.170
Pangaea!

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:00.241
That's kinda what this looks like.

00:01:00.241 --> 00:01:01.773
Okay, there we go.

00:01:01.773 --> 00:01:04.073
That's what I'm talkin' about.

00:01:04.073 --> 00:01:06.345
I'm using the word
rectangle loosely, here,

00:01:06.345 --> 00:01:07.772
because this is a little blobby,

00:01:07.772 --> 00:01:09.212
but it's pretty much a rectangle.

00:01:09.212 --> 00:01:12.452
And now we're gonna
cut it into six strips.

00:01:12.452 --> 00:01:15.126
I was a little skimpy with
this last piece of dough.

00:01:15.126 --> 00:01:17.094
My rationing was a little off.

00:01:17.094 --> 00:01:20.776
I'm skeptical about the amount
of dough it tells you to use,

00:01:20.776 --> 00:01:23.791
because right now, these
strips are pretty thin.

00:01:23.791 --> 00:01:26.117
This is actually a very easy recipe.

00:01:26.117 --> 00:01:27.796
It's basically just making pizza

00:01:27.796 --> 00:01:30.583
in this glorified muffin tin.

00:01:30.583 --> 00:01:33.453
There we go, that's
what I'm talkin' about.

00:01:33.453 --> 00:01:35.673
Now we're gonna fill our Pizza Skulls.

00:01:35.673 --> 00:01:37.151
Sprinkle with a little cheese.

00:01:37.151 --> 00:01:39.343
Define "a little cheese",
though, you know?

00:01:39.343 --> 00:01:41.809
A little cheese to me is
probably a lotta cheese

00:01:41.809 --> 00:01:43.226
to somebody else.

00:01:45.759 --> 00:01:47.860
I'm gonna do half of the skulls with meat,

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:49.317
and half of them without meat.

00:01:49.317 --> 00:01:50.958
Now, I'm just gonna
fill up the rest of the

00:01:50.958 --> 00:01:52.541
skulls with cheese.

00:01:53.854 --> 00:01:55.883
I'm definitely noting
which one is the cheesiest,

00:01:55.883 --> 00:01:57.696
and saving it for myself.

00:01:57.696 --> 00:01:59.905
Now I'm gonna put it in the oven at 375,

00:01:59.905 --> 00:02:01.391
for about 20 minutes.

00:02:01.391 --> 00:02:03.330
The skulls have just come out of the oven.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.026
The dough looks tasty.

00:02:05.026 --> 00:02:07.636
They don't look like
anything from the back side,

00:02:07.636 --> 00:02:09.277
so I have to take them
out of the mold to see

00:02:09.277 --> 00:02:10.895
if it actually looks like a skull.

00:02:10.895 --> 00:02:13.478
(drum rolling)

00:02:15.408 --> 00:02:16.241
Wow!

00:02:17.807 --> 00:02:21.627
You can't see this, but everyone
around me is like (gasp)!

00:02:21.627 --> 00:02:22.843
- [Woman] Those look amazing!

00:02:22.843 --> 00:02:24.319
- Thank you!

00:02:24.319 --> 00:02:25.905
- [Ashley] Will you try my skull pizza?

00:02:25.905 --> 00:02:27.283
- Okay, sure.

00:02:27.283 --> 00:02:28.116
- This is really cute.

00:02:28.116 --> 00:02:31.093
- I would be impressed
already by the look of it.

00:02:31.093 --> 00:02:31.926
- Whoo!

00:02:33.854 --> 00:02:34.797
- Mmmm!

00:02:34.797 --> 00:02:35.630
- I like it.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:36.463
It's hot!

00:02:37.454 --> 00:02:41.119
- Pizza rolls on hydraulics for Halloween.

00:02:41.119 --> 00:02:42.039
This is dope.

00:02:42.039 --> 00:02:44.464
- I did notice that the
ones with meat in them

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:46.699
are much greasier, and
they're a little bit messier,

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:49.042
and the skull doesn't look as clean.

00:02:49.042 --> 00:02:51.862
So if I did this again, I
would probably do just cheese

00:02:51.862 --> 00:02:55.040
and sauce, because these
look really neat and crisp.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.453
Obviously, this goes without saying,

00:02:56.453 --> 00:03:00.036
but the Skull Pizza is
definitely Pin-able.

00:03:01.619 --> 00:03:02.942
(mystical chimes)

00:03:02.942 --> 00:03:04.575
Now onto recipe number two.

00:03:04.575 --> 00:03:07.492
This is Chicken Boo-dle Soup, haha.

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:10.910
I made bow-tie pasta
because it's supposed to

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:12.401
look like a little bats.

00:03:12.401 --> 00:03:14.231
The next step is to dye the pasta black,

00:03:14.231 --> 00:03:16.318
and we're gonna do that
by putting all this pasta

00:03:16.318 --> 00:03:19.627
in a big Ziploc baggy with a
lot of black food coloring,

00:03:19.627 --> 00:03:21.877
and then shaking it around.

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:24.503
There we go.

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:28.094
Now I'm gonna cut the vegetables
into cute little shapes.

00:03:28.094 --> 00:03:31.480
Cut two shallow lines about 1/4 inch

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:32.960
apart from each other.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:33.793
(disk scratching)

00:03:33.793 --> 00:03:36.087
Whoa, okay this blog goes
from peeling and chopping

00:03:36.087 --> 00:03:36.920
Bam!

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:37.753
It's a pumpkin.

00:03:37.753 --> 00:03:39.955
There are a few visuals
that are missing from this.

00:03:39.955 --> 00:03:41.691
Two shallow lines.

00:03:41.691 --> 00:03:43.258
Okay, I think I'm getting it.

00:03:43.258 --> 00:03:44.509
Uh...

00:03:44.509 --> 00:03:46.961
It's not easy like at all.

00:03:46.961 --> 00:03:51.187
So I've kinda got the grooves
that should create the stem.

00:03:51.187 --> 00:03:54.807
Hopefully, pumpkins will emerge
from this but I don't know.

00:03:54.807 --> 00:03:56.383
I'll believe it when I see
it, you know what I'm saying?

00:03:56.383 --> 00:03:59.848
(gasp) No, that's so cute.

00:03:59.848 --> 00:04:00.681
Oh my god.

00:04:01.978 --> 00:04:03.499
Very excited about this.

00:04:03.499 --> 00:04:04.906
That shit is cute.

00:04:04.906 --> 00:04:07.460
And then next, I'm gonna cut the celery,

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:09.031
and I don't really actually
need to do anything,

00:04:09.031 --> 00:04:11.662
'cause when you chop up celery,
it looks like a little moon.

00:04:11.662 --> 00:04:15.512
Celery is not really looking like moon.

00:04:15.512 --> 00:04:17.574
At all. (laughs)

00:04:17.574 --> 00:04:20.407
(energetic music)

00:04:29.424 --> 00:04:31.333
- There is a lot going on.

00:04:31.333 --> 00:04:32.166
- Oh, they're like little pumpkins here.

00:04:32.166 --> 00:04:33.405
Did you cut them?

00:04:33.405 --> 00:04:36.068
- I love the black noodles.

00:04:36.068 --> 00:04:37.503
- I'm scared of the noodles.

00:04:37.503 --> 00:04:38.869
- It's odd.

00:04:38.869 --> 00:04:40.741
- The look is cooler than the taste.

00:04:40.741 --> 00:04:42.336
- This way, it looks like a mushroom.

00:04:42.336 --> 00:04:44.084
When you look at it this way,
it looked like a pumpkin.

00:04:44.084 --> 00:04:46.115
- Chicken Boo-dle Soup is Pin-able.

00:04:46.115 --> 00:04:48.513
(mystical chimes)

00:04:48.513 --> 00:04:50.545
Now, we're onto third and last recipe,

00:04:50.545 --> 00:04:52.715
and those are some deviled
eggs that are meant

00:04:52.715 --> 00:04:54.293
to look like little alien eggs.

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:56.771
Gently crack the hard-boiled
eggs with a knife,

00:04:56.771 --> 00:04:58.650
or by rolling them on the counter.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:02.076
I'm gonna try the counter
method first. (gasp)

00:05:02.076 --> 00:05:05.131
(laughing)

00:05:05.131 --> 00:05:09.379
I was like, "These are never gonna crack!"

00:05:09.379 --> 00:05:12.176
So now we only have five eggs.

00:05:12.176 --> 00:05:14.513
I'm afraid I'm gonna put
my thumb right through

00:05:14.513 --> 00:05:15.757
this whole egg.

00:05:15.757 --> 00:05:16.590
I don't know what to do.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:18.092
Okay, I'm gonna try the knife method.

00:05:18.092 --> 00:05:19.609
(tapping)

00:05:19.609 --> 00:05:21.160
Oh, this works, okay.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:23.429
Looking like little dragon eggs.

00:05:23.429 --> 00:05:26.178
So we boiled our eggs,
we cracked our eggs,

00:05:26.178 --> 00:05:27.200
and now we're gonna color the eggs.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:30.033
(energetic music)

00:05:38.665 --> 00:05:41.539
Now it's time to peel
these eggs and see if

00:05:41.539 --> 00:05:43.330
all of our hard work paid off,

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:46.997
and if this really cool
pattern is on there.

00:05:47.873 --> 00:05:49.623
Wow, that is so cool.

00:05:50.828 --> 00:05:52.318
I'm very happy about this.

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:54.351
Now, basically I'm just
gonna make deviled eggs.

00:05:54.351 --> 00:05:57.184
(energetic music)

00:06:13.004 --> 00:06:13.837
- [Woman] Deviled Alien Eggs?

00:06:13.837 --> 00:06:14.670
I love it.

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:16.510
- These are so pretty.

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:17.570
- How'd you get that pattern?

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:19.937
- That is really good.

00:06:19.937 --> 00:06:21.466
- This would be a crowd pleaser.

00:06:21.466 --> 00:06:24.978
- Very in-theme, but also tastes great.

00:06:24.978 --> 00:06:26.832
I would totally eat this
at a Halloween party.

00:06:26.832 --> 00:06:28.503
I'm really happy about it.

00:06:28.503 --> 00:06:33.005
The Deviled Alien Eggs
are definitely Pin-able.

00:06:33.005 --> 00:06:35.297
I have been on Pinterest
long enough to know

00:06:35.297 --> 00:06:38.630
that there is some Pinterest
BS bein' pinned around there.

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:41.112
But these totally work.

00:06:41.112 --> 00:06:43.234
They were super fun to make,
they tasted really good,

00:06:43.234 --> 00:06:44.736
and they look even cooler.

00:06:44.736 --> 00:06:48.903
What more can you really
ask of a Halloween recipe?

